WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.190
<b>The Autumn of Meiji 14 (1881)</b>

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.200
I'm going to... Saga?

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.790
Right. It's where where 
Master Hibiya was born.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.360
His wife passed away a long while ago,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.460
so it should be a peaceful arrangement.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.410
It's a bit of a relief.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.670
Up against someone like him, even the 
bigwigs couldn't make much of a fuss.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.430
He's got the wisdom of 
age on his side, and...

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.500
Well, I'm sure you know 
better than I can explain.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.850
Proprietor, Madam, you have my thanks.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.520
I really appreciate all you've done for me.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.590
I've never seen a courtesan 
like you before, Yugiri.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.890
I hope I never do again!

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.640
Getting so popular that she 
couldn't get customers...

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.450
How legendary does one girl need to be?

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.610
I'm terribly sorry about that.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.700
I hope you have a good life out there.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.330
But knowing you, I shouldn't need to worry.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:04.480
Oh...

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.010
Oh, come now, what are you girls doing?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.310
Miss Yugiri! Is it true 
you're you're leaving?

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.760
We're not gonna see you again?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.030
Where is Saga? Far away?

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:14.780
I don't like this!

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.620
I wanted you to teach me more 
about singing and dancing!

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.370
There, there, the legendary courtesan is 
going to be setting off to start a new life.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.760
That's nothing to cry about.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.320
Come on. See me off with a smile, all right?

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.950
It doesn't matter how far Saga is.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.830
You're all still going to be in my heart.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.820
Well, technically, Saga doesn't 
really exist anymore.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.310
Even if we have nothing else, 
we still have the future.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:51.210
A lowest point? Starting over from 
zero? That's just part of the saga.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.970
Even if we burn out in the 
process, we'll make it come true!

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.890
This is where our revenge begins!

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:01.390
<b>Zombie Land Saga 
Revenge</b>

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:06.680
<b>The Saga Incident, Part 1</b>

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:18.960
<b>The Spring of Meiji 15 (1882)
The town formerly associated 
with Saga Castle</b>

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.480
Lady Yugiri is so pretty 
every time I see her!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.290
I mean, she's a legendary courtesan!

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.820
What's legendary mean?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.870
You don't need to know.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.320
<i>Several months had passed since the legendary 
courtesan reluctantly left her old life.</i>

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.650
<i>The high-ranking government official</i>

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:58.580
<i>who arranged her freedom passed 
away due to sudden illness.</i>

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.920
<i>In accordance with his wishes,
 she was granted a portion of his fortune.</i>

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.390
<i>Although her well-being was secure,</i>

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.260
<i>she faced the prospect of living 
out the rest of her life</i>

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.410
<i>in a town where she knew
 no one and no one knew her.</i>

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.120
I mean, they have to call 
her a legend for a reason!

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:25.960
She probably puts the folks 
over in Kamiashi-cho to shame.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.340
What made her give up a life like that?

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.640
Come on by and get your fill!

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.710
We've got manju, dango, and shiruko!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.830
Step right on up!

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.790
Th-The time has come for 
us to take a s-stand!

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.450
Saga! Bring back Saga!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.400
Saga!

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.630
Saga?

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.280
What does he want?

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.180
Let's go.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.400
Come on by!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.020
Come on by and have a look!

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.970
It's the Shin Goro traveling show,

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:05.590
and we're in town for a limited 
engagement of only seven days!

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.230
Saga! Saga!

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:09.260
Saga is coming through! Saga!

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.780
Hey! Who the hell are you?!

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.000
S-S-Sorry!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.680
What do you think you're doing?!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.790
S-S-Sorry!

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.380
S-Sorry!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.320
Are you at it again, Kiichi Momozaki?!

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.500
You're not going anywhere this time!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:37.560
Cooperate!

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.020
<b>{zoomed in portion}Homeland...    Where we live...     Not Nagasaki...     Our Saga...</b>

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.860
Paper always has its uses.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.900
You seem dead set on 
always being a nuisance!

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:54.090
You need to give it a rest! 
Do you want to be arrested?

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.130
I can arrest you, y'know!

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.450
I-I just want Saga to be...

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.170
A mugger!

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.150
Don't let him get away!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.340
You stand there and wait for me to get back!

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.540
Where's that mugger?!

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.520
Itou...

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:15.190
You never learn, do you?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:22.500
<i>At the time, Saga was treated as a problem 
prefecture by the Meiji government.</i>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:39.960
<b>Nagasaki</b>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:39.960
<b>Saga</b>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:39.960
<b>Fukuoka</b>

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.130
<i>During the Bakumatsu period, it underwent
 westernization faster than other domains,</i>

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.060
<i>making Saga a key location 
during the reformation...</i>

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.610
<i>But, with uprisings by the former 
samurai class during Meiji 7</i>

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.830
<i>and the accompanying defeats, 
its glory was a thing of the past.</i>

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.620
<i>By Meiji 9, Saga prefecture</i>

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.960
<b>Fukuoka</b>

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.960
<b>Nagasaki</b>

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.960
<b>Mizuma</b>

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.320
<i>had been divided up between the 
prefectures of Mizuma and Nagasaki,</i>

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:48.110
<i>resulting in its total 
erasure from the map.</i>

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:49.680
<b>Nagasaki</b>

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:49.680
<b>Fukuoka</b>

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.130
You need to give it a rest.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.730
I'm not always going to 
be there to help you.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:01.370
I-I'm just trying to bring Saga back, 
the way it should be!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.900
As long as you're making a fuss on your own,

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.470
you're not going to accomplish anything.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.330
The imperial court is still wary of Saga.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:13.810
No one wants a repeat of the Saga War.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:16.160
I'm not trying to start a war!

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.520
That's not what it looks 
like to everyone else.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.140
Besides, even if Saga gets its name back,

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.380
what comes after that?

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.370
I...

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:26.750
Okay, enough of this talk.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.500
Let's set aside the complex stuff

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.210
and go check out the cherry 
blossoms sometime soon.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.130
I guarantee you'll see stuff

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.960
that'll make you forget all about 
this old Saga you're stuck on.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.870
Th-Th-That s-s-s-sort of thing isn't really my...

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.540
Hey, what about my meat?!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.010
Thanks for the meal.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:48.060
Come on out!

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.790
If you've got any confidence 
in your skills, then face me!

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:55.570
You'd be the talk of the town if you didn't 
spend all your time cooped up here, teacher!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.160
The cherry blossoms are in bloom, anyway.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.280
If you'd like, I can tell you 
some places with great views!

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.890
<i>I want you to know what it's 
like in the outside world.</i>

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.260
Wow, look!

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:18.260
Pretty.

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.330
Uh, if this is yours, I, er—

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.790
Thank you kindly.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.860
I just bought it.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.480
Outta the way! Move it, move it, move it!

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.280
Look out!

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.640
Come on, now.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.520
I-I am so—

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.520
Here.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.340
Thanks.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.450
<b><i>We must take Saga back. Saga is our homeland.
Saga is where we were all born.
The land where we live, it is called Saga.
We are not from Mizuma or Nagasaki.
The time has come for us to bring Saga back.
That is why we will rise up for our Saga.</i></b>

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.440
Hey, this is mine...

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.710
Oh, I didn't realize.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.330
I apologize for treating 
it like tissue paper.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.910
You should head on home 
and change into dry clothes.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.000
What're you doing, Kiichi?

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.250
A celestial maiden...

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:27.660
I think I know who you mean.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:32.040
The legendary courtesan who moved 
to Saga around the end of last year.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.750
L-Legendary?

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:36.610
Come on, man, if you want to get Saga back,

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.650
you should probably pay more 
attention to the gossip.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.230
The legendary courtesan, Yugiri.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.890
She was a miracle performer unlike 
anything ever seen in Edo,

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:47.800
idolized by men and women alike.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:52.980
People would bid to be entertained by her so 
competitively that the price got sky-high...

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.420
to the point where no one 
came calling anymore.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.870
The heads of the restoration 
even got into fights over her,

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.960
and there are rumors the Meiji court 
almost fell apart because of it...

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.810
And a person like that... is in Saga?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.780
Don't go falling for her, now.

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:07.950
Wh-Why would I?!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.190
She's not the kind of woman 
a guy like you could handle.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.440
She's from a different world.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.630
A different world...?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.960
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.960
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:56.850
Oh, I remember you.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.540
I'm sorry you went to the trouble.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:12.110
Aw, no, it's nothing fancy... but...

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:14.450
Thank you very much for the gift.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.840
But you should run along, now.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.600
For your own sake.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.420
I... I don't care.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.990
Th-This stuff about you from being 
a different world and like...

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:37.870
All that complicated stuff! 
For our Saga, it's...

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:39.190
In Saga, it's...

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.390
In Saga... it's...

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.430
Pardon me! Does Kiichi Momozaki-han live here?

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:19.810
It's Saga!

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:25.590
I am Saga! No... Saga is me!

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.830
Sir? Are you all right, there?

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:36.170
Gramps, did you run off on...?

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:45.300
It's a herbal medicine that helps with colds and 
other illnesses while being very nourishing.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.300
I had an old acquaintance send it.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.850
I-I appreciate you going 
to all the trouble...

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:56.610
I felt guilty about you braving that blazing 
sun just to show me your gratitude.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:14:00.550
Aw, I only did it because I wanted to...

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.880
It was nice. You were the first 
person to come calling on me,

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.840
other than my dance students, 
since I came to Saga.

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:13.210
Sorry about my grandpa back there...

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.630
He's a little... Well...

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:18.800
He seems like an interesting fellow.

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:26.140
I think Saga losing its name really 
made him worse these last few years...

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:30.140
He started ranting about how 
if he had his old powers,

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:32.880
he'd be able to raise the dead easily...

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:38.840
About eight years ago,
 there was a big battle here in Saga

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.620
and my father was killed.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:48.140
I had nowhere to go and was cowering 
in the wilderness by myself...

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.770
If Gramps hadn't found me,
 I dunno what would've happened.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:55.830
I owe him more than I can ever repay...

00:14:56.070 --> 00:15:02.400
But all he says he wants in 
return is for me to save Saga.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.620
I didn't know what he meant at first...

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.790
But when Saga lost its name,

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:12.590
it felt like everything my father 
tried to protect was going away...

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:16.000
Like Saga was going to vanish 
from inside people's hearts.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.730
<b>We must take Saga back. Saga is our homeland.
Saga is where we were all born.
The land where we live, it is called Saga.
We are not from Mizuma or Nagasaki.
The time has come for us to bring Saga back.
That is why we will rise up for our Saga.</b>

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:18.720
And I didn't want that to happen.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:22.980
I think it's fate that Gramps 
managed to find me...

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.000
So that I could find my way of life.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:33.990
Yugiri, this is where you're 
going to live from now on.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:40.400
I think I can finally picture it.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.540
What I really want to do...

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.960
is create a new Saga.

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:51.620
One where men and women, former samurai 
and peasants, merchants and craftsmen...

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:54.810
A place where everyone can 
choose their own path!

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.780
And live happy lives where 
they're true to themselves!

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:02.470
That's a beautiful dream.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.890
Please! Please, take one!

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:10.620
You wanna be arrested?!

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.370
You want me to arrest you?

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.310
Don't scare me like that!

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.870
<b><i>The time has come to bring back Saga!</i></b>

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.870
<b><i>It has been six years since these lands were made into Mizuma,
 and part of Nagasaki, as a result of the war in the year of Meiji 9.
 But is it truly right for us to claim our home is Nagasaki?
 Can we honestly abide our homeland being stripped of its name?
 What will have become of it, if not?
 We were all born and raised in the land of Saga.
 There is no reason that name should fade away over the course of six years. 
The time has come to appeal to the Imperial Court 
for the return of Saga. Let us all stand together, 
and restore the name of our homeland.</i></b>

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.050
She, uh... helped me clean it up a bit.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:27.450
And helped with the composition and stuff...

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.580
There, there.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:34.510
Come on, now.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.060
It's just some fish.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:02.810
Forgive me. I felt a 
rather... fresh presence.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.490
Sorry!

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.620
I-I know I'm late...

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:10.020
Itou? You're early.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.810
I wanted to meet the legendary 
courtesan as soon as possible.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.370
Here, the big one I caught you.

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:21.450
You actually caught that 
thing in the Fukushoe River?

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:40.850
This is great.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:44.160
I guess the legendary courtesan can cook, 
on top of everything else.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:48.890
The gentleman who arranged for my 
freedom taught me all kinds of things.

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:52.170
Things that would help with 
living in the outside world.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.380
All kinds of things, huh?

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.540
Y'know, maybe it's time for you, too.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.270
What now?

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:04.690
You're not actually that stupid.

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.240
You could become a scholar, or a doctor...

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:10.780
If you want to help people, you could do 
something that's a bit more realistic,

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:14.480
instead of this wild dream 
about bringing Saga back.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:26.580
You met this nice lady. Maybe it 
was a sign to think things over.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.930
Hell, maybe you should think 
of starting a family?

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:34.360
If you're the head of a household, 
you'll feel more responsible, right?

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:36.330
I think it'd suit you.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:45.580
Wh-Wh-What?! What?! What are you, stupid?!

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:49.310
Seriously, what are you— 
What're you trying to—

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.780
Kiichi-han!

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.490
Hang in there, Kiichi-han.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.240
He's helpless, I swear.

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:08.680
Ah, that's all right.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:14.300
How about a drink?

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.450
I'm fine, thank you.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:27.940
Itou-han, have you known 
Kiichi-han for long?

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.340
It was about two years ago...

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.940
I heard there was some oddball 
passing out some strange writings.

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.850
I thought I'd go make fun of him...

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:41.810
I saw how everyone gave him a wide berth, 
without stopping for a second,

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.780
but he kept at it... He was so desperate.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:48.700
There had to have been other ways...

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.700
He's a real fool, to be honest.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:57.530
This country's changed.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.940
It's going to keep changing, too.

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:03.930
What's to be gained by
 clinging to an old name?

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:08.150
I don't think Kiichi-han is 
interested in the old name.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:11.320
He wants to create a new Saga, 
with a fresh start.

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:16.150
It might be a half-formed, shaky dream...

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:21.820
but it's one I'd like to see 
come true. Kiichi-han's Saga.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:34.710
Sooner or later, that earnest 
heart of his is gonna get broken.

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:39.420
This country is still too 
twisted. Too barbaric.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.730
Thanks for the meal. I had a good time.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:56.950
Please take one!

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.740
For Saga...

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:09.530
Excuse me, but could you 
tell us more about this?

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:12.820
We want to get our Saga back, too!

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:25.670
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:27.300
This is Yugiri.

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:31.810
There's always something inspiring about gentlemen 
willing to risk everything for what they believe in.

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:36.420
Next time on Episode 9 of <i>Zombie Land 
Saga Revenge</i>: "The Saga Incident, Part 2."

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>The Saga Incident, Part 2</b>

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:38.080
This is goodbye.
